The warning message "Cannot find the 'CKEDITOR_VERSION' in the 'window' scope" and the issue of CKEditor not loading is likely due to the way CKEditor is being dynamically imported and initialized. To address this, we'll ensure CKEditor is properly imported and loaded. 

### Step 1: Update CKEditorLoaderService

Ensure CKEditor is properly loaded and initialized by updating the `CKEditorLoaderService`:

```typescript
// ckeditor-loader.service.ts
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root',
})
export class CKEditorLoaderService {
  private isCKEditorLoaded = false;

  async loadCKEditor(): Promise<any> {
    if (this.isCKEditorLoaded) {
      return (window as any).ClassicEditor;
    }

    if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
      const { default: ClassicEditor } = await import('@ckeditor/ckeditor5-build-classic');
      (window as any).ClassicEditor = ClassicEditor;
      (window as any).CKEDITOR_VERSION = ClassicEditor.version;
      this.isCKEditorLoaded = true;
      return ClassicEditor;
    }
  }
}
```

