Sure! Subcollections in Firestore are nested collections within a document. They allow you to organize and structure your data hierarchically. Let's go through an example of implementing subcollections and how to query data from them.

### Example Structure

Let's assume we have an `institutes` collection, and each institute document has subcollections for `students` and `teachers`.

### Structure

```
institutes (collection)
  |
  └── instituteId1 (document)
       |
       ├── name: "Institute 1"
       ├── address: "123 Main St"
       ├── startedSince: "2022-01-01"
       |
       ├── students (subcollection)
       |    |
       |    └── studentId1 (document)
       |         ├── name: "Student 1"
       |         ├── email: "student1@example.com"
       |         └── additionalAttribute: "Value"
       |
       └── teachers (subcollection)
            |
            └── teacherId1 (document)
                 ├── name: "Teacher 1"
                 ├── email: "teacher1@example.com"
                 └── additionalAttribute: "Value"
```

### Adding Data to Subcollections

#### Adding an Institute Document

**auth.service.ts**:
```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { Firestore, collection, doc, setDoc } from '@angular/fire/firestore';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class AuthService {
  constructor(private firestore: Firestore) {}

  async addInstitute(instituteId: string, name: string, address: string, startedSince: string): Promise<void> {
    const instituteRef = doc(this.firestore, `institutes/${instituteId}`);
    await setDoc(instituteRef, {
      name,
      address,
      startedSince
    });
  }
}
```

#### Adding a Student to an Institute's Subcollection

**student.service.ts**:
```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { Firestore, collection, doc, setDoc } from '@angular/fire/firestore';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class StudentService {
  constructor(private firestore: Firestore) {}

  async addStudent(instituteId: string, studentId: string, name: string, email: string, additionalAttribute: string): Promise<void> {
    const studentRef = doc(this.firestore, `institutes/${instituteId}/students/${studentId}`);
    await setDoc(studentRef, {
      name,
      email,
      additionalAttribute
    });
  }
}
```

### Querying Data from Subcollections

#### Querying Students of a Specific Institute

**student.service.ts**:
```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { Firestore, collection, collectionData } from '@angular/fire/firestore';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class StudentService {
  constructor(private firestore: Firestore) {}

  getStudentsByInstitute(instituteId: string): Observable<any[]> {
    const studentsRef = collection(this.firestore, `institutes/${instituteId}/students`);
    return collectionData(studentsRef, { idField: 'id' });
  }
}
```

#### Using the Service in a Component

**students.component.ts**:
```typescript
import { Component, OnInit } from '@angular/core';
