The error "ReferenceError: window is not defined" indicates that CKEditor is being accessed during server-side rendering (SSR), where the `window` object is not available. To resolve this, you need to ensure that CKEditor is only used in the browser environment.

Here's a refined approach to address this issue:

### 1. Conditional Loading of CKEditor

Ensure CKEditor is loaded only on the client side.

#### `ckeditor-loader.service.ts`

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root',
})
export class CKEditorLoaderService {
  private isCKEditorLoaded = false;

  async loadCKEditor(): Promise<any> {
    if (this.isCKEditorLoaded) {
      return (window as any).ClassicEditor;
    }

    if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
      const { default: ClassicEditor } = await import('@ckeditor/ckeditor5-build-classic');
      (window as any).ClassicEditor = ClassicEditor;
      this.isCKEditorLoaded = true;
      return ClassicEditor;
    }
  }
}
```

### 2. Update the Component to Use the Service

#### `add-news.component.ts`

```typescript
import { Component, OnInit } from '@angular/core';
import { FormBuilder, FormGroup } from '@angular/forms';
import { CKEditorLoaderService } from './ckeditor-loader.service';

